  "midadHowBody": "Counted from the bundled Uthmani text:\n\n• Letters: diacritics and pause marks are removed; the letter stays as written. “Simple script” folds ٱ أ إ آ into one alef (ا).\n• Words: whole tokens — «الله» is not counted inside «بالله». “Inside words” allows exactly that, explicitly.\n• The divine name: «الله» alone is 2,153, plus «لله» it is 2,703; the familiar 2,699 figure combines them — which is why it differs from the whole-word count.\n• Basmala: not a verse outside Al-Fatihah. The option adds its letters and words, never a verse.\n• Rhyme letter: the last written letter of the verse.\n\nEvery card carries its scope and switches, so every number is reproducible.",
